{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>You shall go out, you and all the people who are at your feet.</b> He says: I and Israel are not leaving your domain until you yourself send us and command us to do so, and after that I will go out. And so here Israel was sent off and released from their imprisonment by supernal power, and therefore from this verse there emerges the known Name for a woman in difficult labor, whose power is mighty to open the restraints of the infant who is bound in the prison house, to bring it forth from confinement into the air of the world, so that it may merit Torah — for a person is born for the labor of Torah, just as Israel came out of their imprisonment to receive the Torah in the third month. And this Name is known to the masters of Names and is public in its pointing. And R. Akiva said: קו\"ף — this is the Holy One, blessed be He; and understand this."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:57:47.690163925Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}